    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301-a6">

                <pb facs="0419" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg345"/>


                <head>Mr. Nelson to Mr. Levenhagen.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santiago de Chili,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-10-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 29, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to submit to your
                    excellency herewith the memorandum of the interview between Admiral Pareja and
                    myself, on board the frigate Villa de Madrid, on the 19th instant, at which you
                    were present. Will you be kind enough, after careful perusal of the same, to
                    state your opinion of its accuracy, and oblige,</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS H. NELSON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles F. Sevenhagen,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé d’ Affaires of Prussia</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
